# M3 review. docs/design.md says an overflow of IST1, the #DF stack, ends
# in a triple fault. The #DF handler here recurses until IST1 runs into its
# guard page. The #PF cannot push its frame there and becomes a #DF, whose
# delivery reloads RSP from the TSS's IST1 slot, the mapped top of IST1: the
# handler runs again over the first one's frames instead. A triple fault
# would end the run with QEMU's own status, not the success exit.
cmdline: test=df_stack
exit: success
expect: microL4 kernel
expect: DF on IST1; recursing until IST1
expect: DF again, frame on IST1
expect: in IST1's guard page: no triple fault
expect: TEST PASS
